{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 3 (near-cap CI leading indicator) implemented and pushed as Gerrit 1751 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1751).\n\nScope: appended a NON-BLOCKING pass to the Module-size gate step in the reusable .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml (the single home both gerrit-verify.yaml and test.yml call). It emits one ::warning:: per src/rebar/**/*.py file within 10% of the locked cap (>= LIMIT - LIMIT/10 = 720 at cap 800) and always exits 0. Band matches code_health.size_near_fraction (0.1) that drives module_size_distribution.near_cap_count. Reuses the gate's own find|wc -l — no second definition of the rule, no new failure mode. Policy note added to docs/architecture.md.\n\nVerification: actionlint clean; YAML parses; local simulation lists 42 in-band files today and the emit loop exits 0; workflow-structure unit tests pass (test_gate_step_tree_skew, test_ci_actionlint_install, test_workflow_names, test_ci_main_push_policy — 135 passed). No Python source touched, so no test-count-parity concern for this change.\n\nBranch akitainu-c3 @ origin/main a79ed876b0. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before submit. Changes 1 (pass1.py split) and 2 (push.py split) next."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786664714744168001,"uuid":"a2f6ddc8-9605-4523-839d-e7151d2db0c0"}